# Word of Command (CR 723.2, 107.3a, 733.1-2): Bot2 is made to cast Earthquake with one Mountain. Bot1 announces X 1, which the
# Mountain can't pay: reversed (`Bot2.Cancel` at the dead end). Each remake with X 1 then ends one question earlier by itself,
# the engine seeing that question's every answer dead - the red mana's assignment, then the Mountain's tap, then X 1's own
# question. Now X 1 is dead, but the X question can't leave out one number between live ones: announced, it is
# refused (`~`), and the question is asked again. X 0 is cast with the Mountain.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Word of Command
Swamp x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Earthquake
Island x18

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Word of Command.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Earthquake)
Bot2.PayCost(X: 1)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Cancel
Bot2.PayCost(X: 1)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.PayCost(X: 1)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.PayCost(X: 1)
~ Bot2.PayCost(X: 1)
Bot2.PayCost(X: 0)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
? Stack = Earthquake
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Earthquake
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 20
